---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a file goes from Files to Paperless
    accDescr: A member of the group of the setting clicks Send to Paperless in the menu of a file or a folder in Files. Nextcloud checks the group, that the user may read each file and that none is in the folder of Paperless Sync, and queues the file, or the files below the folder, at most a batch; files with a marker such as [P123], which Paperless has, stay out. With the next run of cron, the background job asks Paperless for a document with the content of each file, and the sender learns the document if Paperless has one. Otherwise it uploads the file with the tags of the inbox: Paperless refuses it, or the upload fails and waits 15 minutes, then twice as long each time, up to six uploads, or Paperless accepts it. The next runs of cron follow the task of the upload. Every end, a new document, one that Paperless had, a failure or a refusal, reaches the sender as a notification, with a link to the document in Paperless when there is one. The file stays where it is.

    %% The wait takes the uploads that failed for a time back to the upload.
    menu["🖱️ Send to Paperless<br>on a file or folder"]
    queue["Queued: the files<br>that the user may<br>read, at most a batch,<br>none of the app or<br>with a marker"]
    known{"Paperless<br>has the<br>content?"}
    upload{"Upload with<br>the tags of<br>the inbox"}
    retry["Waits 15 minutes,<br>then twice as<br>long, up to<br>6 uploads"]
    task{"Its task,<br>with the next<br>runs of cron"}
    notified["🔔 A notification to the<br>sender: a new document,<br>one that Paperless had,<br>a failure or a refusal,<br>with a link to the<br>document"]

    retry -- "again" --> upload
    menu -- "member of<br>the group" --> queue
    queue -- "next run<br>of cron" --> known
    known -- "yes" --> notified
    known -- "no" --> upload
    upload -- "unreachable<br>or overloaded" --> retry
    upload -- "refused" --> notified
    upload -- "accepted" --> task
    task -- "success, failure,<br>or a day later" --> notified

    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    class menu,queue,retry,notified nextcloud
    class known,upload,task paperless
